        <body>
            <div xml:id="d324">

                <pb facs="0557" n="457" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg457"/>

                <head>No. 324.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Halderman to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bangkok, Siam</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-07-16"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 16, 1884</date>.
                        (Received September 8.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 103.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received this day from his royal
                    highness Prince Krom Mem Nares Warariddhi, the Siamese minister at Washington, a
                    letter of which the inclosed is a copy.</p>
                <p>It will be noted with satisfaction that the embassy were highly pleased at the
                    warm welcome extended to them by the American Government and people.</p>
                <p>Through other channels, strictly personal, the minister prince writes of his
                    journey as a “triumphal march,” a “continued ovation,” whereat he and his suite
                    were made supremely happy.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN A. HALDERMAN.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d324-a1.xml" xpointer="d324-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
